					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-05-06T20:00:00+08:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "wsA52XhEbenKS6lDOMTXSw=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "A failed Mix recompile would normally purge the module being compiled, breaking unrelated files that referenced it.  Each save snapshots loaded project bytecode via `:code.get_object_code/1` and reloads any module Mix purged via `:code.load_binary/3` after the recompile finishes — so an error in one file doesn't cascade across the rest of the project.  See [[Hot-Reload Internals]] for the mechanics."
			}
		]
